 require ... person is entitled to file objections\n\n        and after affording a reasonable <b>opportunity</b> of\n\n        <b>hearing</b>, a final order of <b>assessment</b> has to be passed\n\n        within thirty", "docsize": 57212, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Gujarat High Court", "author": "B Vaishnav", "authorEncoded": "b-vaishnav"}, {"tid": 89468656, "catids": [153], "doctype": 1007, "publishdate": "2021-11-29", "authorid": 1309, "bench": [1309], "title": "Schneider <b>Electric</b> India Pvt.Limited vs The Assistant Commissioner (St) on 29 November, 2021", "numcites": 26, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "Since the said order was passed without affording an\n\n                     <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> to the petitioner, the petitioner had filed ... that the said order was passed in violation\n\n                     of principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b> as no <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> was given to\n\n                     the petitioner. The said", "docsize": 60227, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Madras High Court", "author": "C Saravanan", "authorEncoded": "c-saravanan"}, {"tid": 107041014, "catids": [133], "doctype": 1008, "publishdate": "2012-06-14", "authorid": null, "bench": [273, 165], "title": "M/S Beeco <b>Electrical</b> India And Another vs Pashchimanchal Vidyut Vitran Nigam ... on 14 June, 2012", "numcites": 16, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "sufficient compliance. The Court, however, has said that the principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b> cannot be covered by any strait jacket formula and would depend upon ... <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> was not afforded to him. Besides, the objections filed by petitioner have been considered and discussed in the impugned order of <b>assessment</b>", "docsize": 23229, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court", "citation": "2012 AIR CC 3143 (ALL)"}, {"tid": 41571960, "catids": null, "doctype": 1007, "publishdate": "2025-08-26", "authorid": 1309, "bench": [1309], "title": "S.K.P.Murugaen vs / on 26 August, 2025", "numcites": 14, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "petitioner\n                        submitting his objection to be provisional <b>assessment</b>.\n                                 d. The petitioner shall also given an <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> in\n                        accordance with sub section ... ground that there is a manifest violation of principles\n\n                 of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>.\n \n\n\n                            10.During the interregnum, the petitioner has also been prosecuted and was\n\n                 acquitted", "docsize": 39573, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Madras High Court", "author": "C Saravanan", "authorEncoded": "c-saravanan"}, {"tid": 21517510, "catids": null, "doctype": 1007, "publishdate": "2024-03-07", "authorid": 1321, "bench": [1321], "title": "P.Ramamoorthi vs The Superintending Engineer on 7 March, 2024", "numcites": 7, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>assessment</b> of theft of <b>electricity</b>.\n\n                     Further, this Court has noted that the petitioner was present and\n\n                     submitted his defense statement and <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> ... given to\n\n                     him and there is no violation of principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>. Even in\n\n                     Form 91 of the FIR, it is noted that theft", "docsize": 19222, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Madras High Court", "author": "J N Banu", "authorEncoded": "j-n-banu"}, {"tid": 72075776, "catids": null, "doctype": 1017, "publishdate": "2023-03-20", "authorid": 862, "bench": [862], "title": "Narendrabhai Parshotambhai Makwana vs State Of Gujarat on 20 March, 2023", "numcites": 10, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "thereafter    recovery         notice,   without       providing          an\n<b>opportunity</b>         of   <b>hearing</b>    to     the     petitioner,   at     the      time     of\n<b>assessment</b> of supplementary bill and even thereafter, which ... Section\n126  of the Act and also against the principle of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>\nand the position of law as held in the case of Jayshree", "docsize": 29064, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Gujarat High Court", "author": "V Nanavati", "authorEncoded": "v-nanavati"}, {"tid": 104138087, "catids": null, "doctype": 1017, "publishdate": "2023-03-20", "authorid": 862, "bench": [862], "title": "Narendrabhai Parshotambhai Makwana vs State Of Gujarat on 20 March, 2023", "numcites": 10, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "thereafter    recovery         notice,   without       providing          an\n<b>opportunity</b>         of   <b>hearing</b>    to     the     petitioner,   at     the      time     of\n<b>assessment</b> of supplementary bill and even thereafter, which ... Section\n126  of the Act and also against the principle of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>\nand the position of law as held in the case of Jayshree", "docsize": 29069, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Gujarat High Court", "author": "V Nanavati", "authorEncoded": "v-nanavati"}, {"tid": 62618930, "catids": [629], "doctype": 1008, "publishdate": "2015-10-07", "authorid": null, "bench": [197, 143], "title": "M/S Sartaj Rice Mill Thru' Its Partner ... vs Paschimanchal Vidhyut Vitran Nigam ... on 7 October, 2015", "numcites": 7, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>assessment</b> has to be made after providing an <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> to the petitioner to submit his case so that the cases of <b>assessment</b> ... <b>Electric</b> Distribution Division-II, Rampur, hence it cannot be said that the order is ex parte or in violation of the principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>", "docsize": 30226, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court"}, {"tid": 862164, "catids": [61, 44, 46], "doctype": 1005, "publishdate": "2006-04-18", "authorid": 541, "bench": [541], "title": "Zenath Parveen vs Cesc Ltd. And Ors. on 18 April, 2006", "numcites": 10, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "fraudulent case. The provisional <b>assessment</b> was made on an imaginary ground. The so-called <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> given to the writ petitioner without furnishing copies ... provisional <b>assessment</b> and final <b>assessment</b> should be set aside and the CESC Ltd. should be directed to restore supply of <b>electricity</b> forthwith.\n  \n\n  7. Mr. Bose", "docsize": 24424, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Calcutta High Court", "author": "G C Gupta", "authorEncoded": "g-c-gupta", "citation": "(2006)2CALLT579(HC)"}, {"tid": 139824819, "catids": null, "doctype": 1033, "publishdate": "2025-08-11", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "Ronda Pattabhi Ramiredd vs The Ap Central Power Distribution ... on 11 August, 2025", "numcites": 7, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "declare that\nsuch demands, raised without prior notice, proper <b>assessment</b>, or affording an\n<b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b>, are barred by limitation; and consequently set aside ... Constitution of\nIndia, the principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>, and contrary to  Section 56(2)  of the\n<b>Electricity</b> Act, 2003.\nlA NO: 1 OF 2025\n\n      Petition", "docsize": 8641, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Andhra Pradesh High Court - Amravati"}], "found": "31 - 40 of 2291", "encodedformInput": "electricity%20assessment%20%22opportunity%20of%20hearing%22%20natural%20justice%20doctypes%3Ahighcourts"}